 "ref": "The plea agreement has a word for what came next. He acted, it says, to lull the investors into believing their funds were safely invested. Horwitz admitted he falsely reassured investors that the missed payments were caused by the streaming platforms, and that payments would resume. He sent investors emails and text messages that he claimed came from representatives of the platforms. In fact, he admitted, he had not been in communication with the platforms, and the correspondence was fake. Prosecutors later said those messages used the identities of actual H-B-O and Netflix employees. He had been charged with aggravated identity theft, but those counts were dismissed under his plea deal, and he was not convicted of them.",
